services/README.md
# A Quick Start Guide

This guide provides instructions for running the SCX schedulers as a systemd service and checking its logs.

## Getting Started

At the very beginning, configure the /etc/default/scx file:

- in the SCX_SCHEDULER variable, select the scheduler you are interested in

- in the SCX_FLAGS variable, specify the flags you want to add. To do this, execute and read what flags you can add.

```
scx_SCHEDNAME --help
```

To start the SCX scheduler at boot, you need to run the systemd service as root. Here are the steps:


- Enable the service:

```
systemctl enable scx.service
```

- Start the service:

```
systemctl start scx.service
```

Alternatively, you can use a shortened version of these commands:

```
systemctl enable --now scx.service
```

- To check the status of the service, use the following command:

```
systemctl status scx.service
```

## Override global configuration

It is possible to override the global scx settings using systemd environment
variables `SCX_SCHEDULER_OVERRIDE` and `SCX_FLAGS_OVERRIDE`.

Example:

```
systemctl set-environment SCX_SCHEDULER_OVERRIDE=scx_rustland
systemctl set-environment SCX_FLAGS_OVERRIDE="-s 10000"
systemctl restart scx
```

If you want to restore the default value from the `/etc/default/scx` file execute:

```
systemctl unset-environment SCX_SCHEDULER_OVERRIDE
systemctl unset-environment SCX_FLAGS_OVERRIDE
systemctl restart scx
```

## Checking journald Logs


- To view the logs, use the following command:

```
journalctl -u scx.service
```

- To view the logs of the current session use the command

```
journalctl -u scx.service -b 0
```

services/anima-hypr.service
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# AnimaSchedEXT — Hyprland focus daemon (systemd USER service)
#
# Subscribes to Hyprland's activewindowv2 events and pushes the focused
# PID into scx_lavd's pinned anima_active_pids BPF map. LAVD then gives
# that PID the tightest virtual deadline (see anima.bpf.h).
#
# Why a user service (not a system service)?
#   The daemon needs HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE and XDG_RUNTIME_DIR to
#   talk to the Hyprland IPC socket. These env vars are only present in
#   the user's graphical session — a system service can't see them
#   without ugly passthrough hacks. Plus the pins are chmod 666 so no
#   root/CAP_BPF is required to update the maps.
#
# Install:
#   install -Dm644 anima-hypr.service ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#   systemctl --user enable --now anima-hypr.service
#
# Logs:
#   journalctl --user -u anima-hypr.service -f

[Unit]
Description=AnimAIOS Hyprland focus daemon (scx_lavd boost)
PartOf=graphical-session.target
After=graphical-session.target

[Service]
Type=simple
# window+tree: boost focused PID + its low-CPU direct children. Switch to
# just "window" if you want the focused process only (no descendants).
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/anima-hypr-daemon window+tree
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=3

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical-session.target
services/anima-scx-loader.conf
# Drop-in for scx_loader.service — swap in the AnimaSchedEXT build of
# scx_lavd (the one that pins anima_active_pids for the focus daemon).
#
# Place at /etc/systemd/system/scx_loader.service.d/anima.conf

[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/scx_lavd-anima --performance
Restart=on-failure
services/anima.conf
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# tmpfiles.d snippet for AnimaSchedEXT
#
# Creates /run/anima on boot so the user daemon can bind its tab socket
# without needing root. The directory is world-writable so any browser
# native-messaging host (which runs as the user) can connect.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -Dm644 anima.conf /etc/tmpfiles.d/

d /run/anima 0777 root root -
services/scx
# List of scx_schedulers: scx_beerland scx_bpfland scx_chaos scx_cosmos scx_flash scx_lavd scx_p2dq scx_rustland scx_rusty scx_tickless
SCX_SCHEDULER=scx_cosmos

# Set custom flags for each scheduler, below is an example of how to use
SCX_FLAGS='-s 700 -S'
services/scx.service
[Unit]
Description=Start scx_scheduler
ConditionPathIsDirectory=/sys/kernel/sched_ext
StartLimitIntervalSec=30
StartLimitBurst=2

[Service]
Type=simple
EnvironmentFile=/etc/default/scx
ExecStart=/bin/bash -c 'exec ${SCX_SCHEDULER_OVERRIDE:-$SCX_SCHEDULER} ${SCX_FLAGS_OVERRIDE:-$SCX_FLAGS} '
Restart=on-failure
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

