**Audit Result**

This repo has **not** been purged to LAVD-only content.

Obvious non-LAVD scheduler components still tracked:

- `scheds/rust/scx_beerland`
- `scheds/rust/scx_bpfland`
- `scheds/rust/scx_cake`
- `scheds/rust/scx_chaos`
- `scheds/rust/scx_cosmos`
- `scheds/rust/scx_flash`
- `scheds/rust/scx_layered`
- `scheds/rust/scx_mitosis`
- `scheds/rust/scx_p2dq`
- `scheds/rust/scx_pandemonium`
- `scheds/rust/scx_rustland`
- `scheds/rust/scx_rusty`
- `scheds/rust/scx_tickless`
- `scheds/experimental/scx_flow`
- `scheds/experimental/scx_rlfifo`
- `scheds/experimental/scx_wd40`

Workspace/config still includes them in [Cargo.toml](/home/vi/animaschedext/Cargo.toml:13), and [Cargo.lock](/home/vi/animaschedext/Cargo.lock:3624) still has package entries for the removed candidates.

Other obvious non-LAVD leftovers:

- [scheds/rust/README.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/README.md:15) lists all Rust schedulers.
- [services/scx](/home/vi/animaschedext/services/scx:1) lists many schedulers and defaults to `scx_cosmos`.
- [services/README.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/services/README.md:52) documents generic SCX service usage and `scx_rustland`.
- [CARGO_BUILD.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/CARGO_BUILD.md:69), [UNIT_TESTING_GUIDE.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/UNIT_TESTING_GUIDE.md:35), [DHQ_README.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/DHQ_README.md:709), [RELEASE.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/RELEASE.md:129), and parts of [INSTALL.md](/home/vi/animaschedext/INSTALL.md:105) reference non-LAVD schedulers.
- `tools/scxcash` is visibly `scx_layered`-oriented in its BPF map naming.
- `tools/scxtop` is generic sched_ext tooling with examples/tests referencing `scx_rusty` and `scx_layered`.

If the fork should focus only on `scx_lavd` / anima LAVD, deletion would likely include the non-LAVD scheduler directories above, removal of their workspace members from `Cargo.toml`, regenerating `Cargo.lock`, and pruning or rewriting generic SCX docs/services/tooling so only `scx_lavd`, `scx_lavd-anima`, `anima-hypr-daemon`, and `animatab` remain.

I would not blindly delete shared infrastructure yet: `scx_lavd` directly depends on `rust/scx_arena`, `rust/scx_cargo`, `rust/scx_stats`, `rust/scx_stats_derive`, and `rust/scx_utils`; `scheds/include` and `scheds/vmlinux` also look like shared BPF/kernel build support.

No intentional file edits were made. `git status --short` shows an untracked `docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log`, which appears to be session logging rather than a source edit.
